 "asked_at": "2026-10-17T12:45+08:00",
 "answer": "**Probably okay for a short, easy ride if you’re generally healthy—but I’d skip a hard or long ride, especially if the haze is obvious where you are.**\n\nThe latest Kuching station reading I found for **Saturday, October 17** was **API 65 (moderate) at 11 a.m.** That’s below Malaysia’s unhealthy threshold of 101, but it may have changed by evening. Cycling can mean breathing in more pollution because you’re exerting yourself. ([hazemonitor.com](https://hazemonitor.com/station/kuching?utm_source=openai))\n\nCheck the DOE’s APIMS reading before heading out. If the API reaches **100 or higher**, or you can see or smell smoke, choose an indoor workout instead. Be extra cautious if you have asthma or heart or lung problems. Also, thunderstorms are forecast this evening, so check local weather and avoid riding in rain or lightning. ([nadma.gov.my](https://www.nadma.gov.my/bm/media-2/berita/6907-got-haze-health-worries-ministry-steps-up-monitoring-medical-readiness?utm_source=openai))",
